// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/trinet/tern_tc_reopen_long_ax7203.t27 -- pre-registration: the 32-token igla-coder
; generation on the AX7203 node, with retransmits and the serial port closed and opened again when
; a resync meets a silent line
; The one source for this run. conformance/tern_tc_reopen_long_from_spec.mjs compiles this file with
; the t27 compiler (wasm), evaluates every test block below, checks the pinned files, reads back the
; constants it repeats from the long generation and retransmit specs' generated params, and writes
; conformance/tern_tc_reopen_long_params.py, which the wrapper
; conformance/tern_tc_generate_reopen_long_ax7203.py reads. The wrapper installs the long parameters
; under the module names the pinned runners read (tern_tc_generate_params, tern_tc_reopen_params)
; and then imports the unchanged runner conformance/tern_tc_generate_reopen_ax7203.py, so every
; --self-test, --refcell, preflight and board byte runs the pinned code. `--check` fails on drift.
; Written 2026-09-28 before any run of it. ASCII, English.

; WHY. The 8-token reopen run (conformance/TERN_TC_REOPEN.md, PASS 7682304/7682304, 0 bytes lost,
; 0 reopens needed) proved the harness on the hub-free DIRECT UART. T34 asks for longer generation:
; 32 tokens, 30762752 answers, 584492288 answer bytes. That is 4x the answers of any run so far and
; 1.3x the hub-free loss-free evidence itself (23385600 answers, conformance/UART_LOSS_HUBFREE.md),
; so at this length a lost byte is expected somewhere behind any adapter, and the reopen link is the
; only harness that has survived one (the retransmit-only run died in call 145 of 192 on exactly
; that). This is a new claim with its own record, conformance/TERN_TC_GENERATE_LONG.md.

; WHAT CHANGES FROM THE 8-TOKEN REOPEN RUN. Only the length, through the long generation spec's
; parameters: N_TOKENS 32, JOBS_EXPECTED 30762752, and LIMIT_S 13500 (the 8-token arm's 3600 s
; ceiling is 4x too small for 4x the tokens; the change is stated here, not hidden). Every link,
; protocol, ceiling, window and key-handling byte is the 8-token reopen run's, imported unchanged
; and pinned below. The token ids and every count the run must equal are the long generation spec's
; (specs/trinet/tern_tc_generate_long_ax7203.t27), fixed on the CPU before this file was written.

; WHAT IS NEVER RETRIED (the run stops). Everything the 8-token reopen spec lists: MAX_ATTEMPTS
; nonces per job, a reopen past MAX_REOPENS, and every receipt lie.

; PREDICTION (board). Token ids == CPU_INT_IDS of the long generation spec; every one of
; JOBS_EXPECTED jobs credited by exactly one answer whose tag verifies under the node key; every
; row bit-exact; retransmits <= MAX_RETRANSMITS; resyncs <= MAX_RESYNCS; reopens <= MAX_REOPENS;
; one node id throughout; elapsed <= LIMIT_S. The runner prints `receipts verified (tag) : N/N`
; only then. 32 tokens cross the entry into the model's period-8 repeat loop (tokens 16-31); the
; loop is the CPU paths' own behavior, fixed in the long generation spec, not a board property.
; PREDICTION (rehearsal, no board). The whole 32-token run through the reference cell behind the
; RTL's frame parser, with the retransmit spec's five losses and the two stalls below, ends
; REHEARSAL OK with the same ids and counts, at least one retransmit per scheduled loss, and
; exactly REHEARSAL_STALLS reopens: one per stall, none for the ordinary losses. The stalls keep
; the 8-token rehearsal's offsets: the mechanism a reopen clears is position-independent byte
; counters, and keeping the schedule means the new thing this rehearsal tests is length -- after
; the reopen at answer 5754002 the run must continue to 30762752 and stay bit-exact.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. It does not find which side stalls or loses. It does not say the UART is
; lossless. It is not speed and not text quality (the ids repeat; the long generation spec says
; why). One attempt; a second only if the first fails before its first job, and then both are
; recorded.

module trinet_tern_tc_reopen_long_ax7203;

pub const KIND : str = "board-run-preregistration";
pub const ID : str = "trinet/tern_tc_reopen_long_ax7203";
pub const GENERATED : [1]str = ["conformance/tern_tc_reopen_long_params.py"];
pub const RUNNER : str = "conformance/tern_tc_generate_reopen_long_ax7203.py";
pub const RECORD_DOC : str = "conformance/TERN_TC_GENERATE_LONG.md";
pub const LOG_NAME : str = "gen_tokens_32_reopen";

; --- Code and data of record: imported or read, never edited --------------------------------
